# core/data/talk/grammar/en/actions.tlk - TM2e: the lines that say a sim action is being done (owner: TK;
# docs/TALK.md 6o; design TALK_MULTILEVEL 6.1 and 10). Each is a second line by the same resident, said only
# when the drama manager has added the event the line promises (talk_gen_action; talk_outcome_apply does it):
#   act.start     the invitation was accepted and the resident really goes (sim_nudge_activity)
#   act.ask_item  the resident asks the player for their favourite food (PROB_WANTS_ITEM)
#   act.call      the resident goes to get someone and the scene lets them into the room
#   hook.gift (in hooks.tlk)  the resident hands over a snack (inv_add)
# Kid-safe everywhere: a place, a snack, a friend. No register word, no romance, nothing to a child alone.
# The guard `hook=` is set by the generator.

@rule act.start guard: hook=start&topic act: ask_about
  "Okay, {x} it is. Race you there!"
  "Deal! Let's go to {x}. Come on!"
  "Yes! Off to {x}, then. Follow me!"
  "{x:cap}? Say no more. I'm already walking!"
  "Fine, {x}. I'm in. Let's move!"
@rule act.start.open guard: hook=start&!topic act: ask_about
  "Okay, I know a spot. Follow me!"
  "Deal! My pick of places. Come on!"
  "Sure thing. Let's go somewhere fun!"
  "Say no more. I'm already heading out."
@rule act.ask_item guard: hook=item act: ask_about
  "Got any {food} on you, {you}? I'd be so happy."
  "I'm dreaming of {food}. Do you have some?"
  "Psst, {you}. Any {food} in your bag?"
  "Could you bring me some {food}? Please?"
@rule act.call guard: hook=caller act: ask_about
  "Hang on, I'll wave someone over."
  "Wait here. I'll go get a friend."
  "This needs more people. Let me call someone over."
  "The more the merrier. Be right back!"
  "Hold that thought. I'm fetching someone."
  "I know who'd love this. Back in a sec!"
